#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Extract the working draft's examples as accept/reject tests (tests/draft/README.md, #6).

    tools/draft-examples              regenerate tests/draft from the pinned draft, the pinned CWG
                                      list and the recorded oracle verdicts (tests/draft/oracles.tsv)
    tools/draft-examples --oracles    also run Clang 23 and GCC 16 on every example and record
                                      their verdicts; needs both (tests/driver/toolchain.py)
    tools/draft-examples --pin-draft SHA --pin-cwg SHA
                                      move a pin (cplusplus/draft main, cplusplus/CWG gh-pages)

The pins are in tests/draft/PINS. The sources are downloaded once into build/spec-cache.

Every example (`\\begin{example}`) of the core-language clauses becomes one test named by its
subclause's stable name and its index there (`tests/draft/temp/temp.deduct.call-3.reject.cpp`),
or one line in tests/draft/examples.tsv saying why it is skipped. A line whose comment gives an
ill-formed verdict ("error", "ill-formed", "ambiguous", ...: annotation()) gets an `//! error`
marker; an example with such a line is a reject test, any other an accept test. Standard headers
the example takes for granted are included at its top (Example.prelude()).

The oracles decide only two things: whether an example is a fragment (both report errors on
lines the draft does not annotate, of the kind an incomplete example produces), and which oracle
gets an `XFAIL` because it disagrees with the draft. Each disagreement is a row of
tests/draft/DISAGREEMENTS.md, next to the CWG issues filed against that subclause.
"""
